    intro: "A material substitution is a design and production change, not just a purchasing convenience. Two products with the same nominal name can differ in actual thickness, usable size, core, face, finish, flatness, machining behavior, fastener performance, edge treatment, availability, and appearance. The workflow should define who may approve the alternative, which evidence is required, which parts and layouts change, and how the revised product is identified through receiving, cutting, assembly, and installation.",
